{
  "A short description shown next to an element: after the pointer rests on it, when it gets keyboard focus, or programmatically. It can be hovered, Escape hides it, and one is open at a time on the page.": "",
  "In JSX a tooltip is placed anywhere and pointed at its `target`; where it sits does not matter. Programmatically, `new Tooltip({ target, text })` needs nothing else: it puts itself into the page when it first shows, and goes when its target component does.": "",
  "Icon-only buttons": "",
  "A button with only an icon needs its own name (`aria-label`); the tooltip shows it to sighted users and adds the shortcut as a description. Moving from one button to the next shows the next tooltip at once.": "",
  "On a field": "",
  "On a TextBox the whole field shows it on hover, and its input is described by it while it shows, also on keyboard focus.": "",
  "`top` by default. It opens on the other side when there is no room, and `start` / `end` follow the reading direction (try the RTL switch at the top).": "",
  "The pointer rests `delay` milliseconds on the target before it shows (500 by default); `hideDelay` keeps it a moment after the pointer leaves. Right after one closed, the next shows at once (`Tooltip.skipDelay`).": "",
  "Rich content": "",
  "JSX children or `content` (any component) come after the text. Keep it short and never put buttons or links in it: a tooltip cannot take focus.": "",
  "When it shows": "",
  "`showOn` picks what shows it: `hover-focus` (default), `focus` (keyboard focus only) or `manual` (only `open()` / `opened`). `enabled` turns a tooltip off.": "",
  "Many elements": "",
  "`addTooltip(target, text)` gives an element a tooltip that is made only when it is first needed; every tooltip on the page shares one set of document listeners, so hundreds of them cost next to nothing. It returns the function that removes it.": "",
  "Shows it at once; leaving the target hides it.": "",
  "Hides it; focus stays where it is. Only the tooltip closes, not the window around it.": "",
  "`role=\"tooltip\"`, one element per tooltip.": "",
  "While it is shown the target (its focusable part, e.g. the input of a TextBox) has `aria-describedby` pointing to it, next to its own descriptions.": "",
  "It never takes focus and holds nothing interactive. For buttons or links next to an element, open a drop-down (Button `dropDown`).": "",
  "Dismissible (Escape), hoverable (the pointer can move onto it) and persistent (it stays until the pointer or focus leaves).": "",
  "Never: whatever it says must also be reachable without it. An icon-only button still needs its own name (`aria-label`).": "",
  "A touch does not show it; give touch users the information another way.": "",
  "The tooltip. `data-side` tells the side it opened on (`top`, `bottom`, `start`, `end`).": "",
  "The gap to its target, and how far it comes in from it.": "",
  "Unit: the tooltip with its box (`max-width`: the widest it gets before it wraps; `rich`: with content of its own).": "",
  "Units: an arrow towards the target a design may show, and the text.": "",
  "How its text lines up.": "",
  "What it describes. A function is fine for a component that comes later in the view (`() => this.save`).": "",
  "What it says.": "",
  "Any content after the text, made the first time it shows. JSX children work too. Nothing interactive.": "",
  "`top`, `bottom`, `start`, `end`, each with `-start` / `-end`. It opens on the other side when there is no room; start and end follow the reading direction.": "",
  "Milliseconds the pointer rests on the target before it shows. Keyboard focus shows it at once.": "",
  "Milliseconds it stays after the pointer leaves, so the pointer can move onto it.": "",
  "`hover-focus`, `focus` (keyboard focus only), `manual` (only `open()`).": "",
  "`false`: it never shows, and closes if it is open.": "",
  "See Events.": "",
  "Whether it is shown; setting it opens or closes it.": "",
  "Milliseconds after a tooltip closes during which the next one shows at once (default `300`; `0` turns it off).": "",
  "Shows it now, whatever `showOn` says; `false` without a target on the page, or when disabled.": "",
  "Hides it.": "",
  "Lines it up with its target again, e.g. after the target moved.": "",
  "A tooltip for one element, made on first use; returns the function that removes it. For a component it goes with the component.": "",
  "It was hidden.": ""
}
